* BREAK DEMO
* -----------
* Parses a pipe-delimited record into three fields using the BREAK pattern.
*   BREAK('|')      matches everything up to (but not including) the next '|'
*   . NAME          binds the matched substring to the variable NAME
*   REM             matches the remainder of the subject
*   :F(NO)          on match failure, branch to label NO
* If parsing succeeds we print NAME, SEX, MAJOR; otherwise "parse failed".
       LINE = 'Alice|F|English'
       LINE BREAK('|') . NAME '|' BREAK('|') . SEX '|' REM . MAJOR :F(NO)
       OUTPUT = NAME
       OUTPUT = SEX
       OUTPUT = MAJOR :(END)
NO     OUTPUT = 'parse failed'
END
